+{"ts":1768725812484,"seq":15783,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KF7T27BXD9SNG1ZR4PV63S57","data":{"iteration":1,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"stdout":"> @kynetic/spec@0.1.0 dev\n> tsx src/cli/index.ts item get @spec-completeness\n\nSpec Completeness Validation\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KF3GST2YDS6MA1A04WK7A9FJ\nSlugs:     spec-completeness\nType:      requirement\nMaturity:  draft\nImplementation: implemented\n\n─── Description ───\nValidation checks for spec quality beyond schema conformance. Warns about incomplete specs to help maintain spec-as-source-of-truth principle.\n\n─── Acceptance Criteria ───\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: A spec item exists without acceptance_criteria\n    When: kspec validate --completeness runs\n    Then: A warning is shown: 'Item @slug has no acceptance criteria'\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: A spec item exists without a description\n    When: kspec validate --completeness runs\n    Then: A warning is shown: 'Item @slug has no description'\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: A parent item has implementation:implemented but children have not_started\n    When: kspec validate --completeness runs\n    Then: A warning is shown about status inconsistency between parent and children\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: Multiple completeness issues exist\n    When: kspec validate --completeness runs\n    Then: A summary is shown with counts by issue type (e.g., '3 items missing AC, 2 status mismatches')","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_014qWgofxDYLnmbEV3w25sRs","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
